/// Behavioral API documentation for the Roadie Roster backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source; reads no state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Roadie Roster Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nBackend for **Roadie Roster**, the new-hire tracking app for Bubba's 33 store #975 in Lake Charles, LA (opening Mon Feb 8, 2027). It stores store configuration, positions (stations) with build-to targets, the opening schedule, checklists, retention settings, roadie cards, kiosk sign-up submissions, access grants, the admin-set kiosk PIN, and the phase-2/3 records (orientation check-off, attendance, training groups, trainer notes, leader talks, final sign-offs, alerts).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes application data requires a **signed (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nSigning in is not enough: a principal must be **registered** before any role-guarded call succeeds. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `requestAccess()` once. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n- `requestAccess()` records the caller in the pending list and returns `true` when the caller is already registered (or already pending). It is safe to call repeatedly.\n- An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap on every guarded endpoint: `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- A Kiosk login receives `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up` on every read.\n- An expired access grant (past its access end date) is treated as unregistered.\n\n### First-admin bootstrap\n\n`bootstrapAdmin()` bridges the platform's shared authorization grant into the app's access model. It succeeds only while no app admin exists and only for the platform's first user; it returns `true` when the caller holds an app Admin grant after the call. `adminCount()` reports the number of non-expired admins.\n\n## Roles and authorization\n\nRoles: `admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `leadership`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `kiosk`, `integration`.\n\n- **Admin** — full access; the only role that may manage access grants, store configuration, positions, schedule, checklists, retention, and the kiosk PIN.\n- **Store Manager** — manager-level access: roadie cards with contact sets, sign-up approval, build-to adjustment, trainer notes, exports.\n- **Trainer** — sees only roadies in the stations listed in their grant's `trainerPositionIds`; a trainer with no stations sees no roadies. Trainer notes are restricted the same way.\n- **Integration** — sees only the Shareable export; every roadie card, change-log entry, and trainer-note read returns nothing.\n- **Kiosk** — may only submit a sign-up; every read traps.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Timestamps** are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (matching `Time.now()`).\n- **Date-only** values are UTC-midnight nanosecond timestamps; exactly zero means \"not set\". A negative value is a real pre-1970 date and is handled correctly by the age helpers.\n- **Identifiers** (`RoadieId`, `PositionId`, `EventId`, `CrewId`, `SignupId`, `ChangeLogId`, `TrainingGroupId`, `LeaderTalkId`, `AlertId`) are `Nat`.\n- **PhotoRef** and **SignatureRef** are platform file-storage references (blob bytes), not text. Fetch a roadie photo with `getPhoto(id)` and a sign-up photo with `getSignupPhoto(id)`; both return `null` when absent or not visible.\n- **Availability** is a list of `{ day, shift }` cells; `day` is one of `wed..tue` and `shift` is `am` or `pm`.\n- **isMinor** and **birthdayMonthDay** are non-sensitive derived values recomputed on every read from the contact-set date of birth in the store time zone, so a roadie who turns 18 stops being flagged as a minor on the next read. `birthdayMonthDay` is `\"MM-DD\"` or `null`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `getMyAccess()` returns the caller's own grant, or `null` until an Admin approves them. The frontend polls it while showing the waiting screen; treat `null` as \"still waiting\", not an error.\n- `listPendingSignups()` returns only `#pending` submissions and never includes photo bytes.\n- `getRosterSummary()` returns per-position `{ positionId, positionName, onHand, buildTo, openSpots }`; on-hand counts each roadie once under their main position only.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `requestAccess()` is idempotent.\n- `approveSignup(id, ...)` traps when the submission has already been decided; a retry after success is rejected rather than creating a second roadie.\n- `approveUser(request)` traps when the principal has no pending request; it removes the pending entry on success.\n- `archiveRoadie` requires a reason; `rehireRoadie` requires a non-blank reason. `updateRoadieStatus` can never set or clear `#archived`.\n- `updateAccessEnd` refuses **any** end date (past or future) on an admin grant, and an Admin grant is always stored with no end date. `updateUserRole` and `removeUser` refuse to leave zero active admins.\n- `adjustBuildTo` applies a signed delta to the stored build-to targets and records a `BuildToAdjustment`.\n\n## Kiosk PIN\n\n- `setKioskPin(pin)` (Admin only) stores only a one-way hash of the PIN; the plaintext is never persisted or returned. An empty PIN traps.\n- `checkKioskPin(pin)` returns `true` when the candidate matches the stored hash; it is a query callable by any caller so the kiosk can gate entry.\n- `hasKioskPin()` returns `true` once an Admin has set a PIN.\n\n## Exports\n\n- `buildShareableExport()` (any read-capable role) returns the export with **no** contact set and **empty** availability arrays, so it never leaks availability.\n- `buildFullExport()` (Admin/Store Manager only) fills the whole contact set, availability by shift and by day, and records a `buildFullExport` change-log entry.\n- Both fill the overview totals: `fohTotalPar`/`bohTotalPar`/`grandTotalPar` and the matching `*Need` fields.\n\n## Errors and traps\n\n- Unregistered or expired callers trap with `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- Missing role traps name the required role, e.g. `Access denied: Admin role required`.\n- Missing records trap with a message such as `Roadie not found` or `Position not found`.\n- A roadie below a position's minimum age traps on `approveSignup` and `changePosition`.\n";
  };
};
